00:34:31,361 --> 00:34:33,738
We've put the terms
we agreed on in the contract.

520
00:34:34,030 --> 00:34:35,031
Go over it and let me know.

521
00:34:35,907 --> 00:34:38,118
I see. Okay.

522
00:34:38,577 --> 00:34:39,578
I'll get going now.

523
00:34:48,336 --> 00:34:50,171
This is driving me crazy.

524
00:34:50,422 --> 00:34:53,300
So did she say
she'd review the new contract?

525
00:34:53,717 --> 00:34:54,718
Yes.

526
00:34:55,719 --> 00:34:57,679
But I don't know
if she'll actually take it.

527
00:34:58,054 --> 00:34:59,931
Of course she will.
There's no reason not to.

528
00:35:00,015 --> 00:35:01,558
It's brand marketing.

529
00:35:05,270 --> 00:35:08,023
But isn't Gong Yeon-su kind of cute?

530
00:35:10,984 --> 00:35:12,193
What do you mean?

531
00:35:12,277 --> 00:35:15,280
She's not exactly the type of person
that fits in at our company.

532
00:35:15,363 --> 00:35:17,741
But she bustles around
trying to make things work.

533
00:35:17,824 --> 00:35:18,825
I find it cute.

534
00:35:20,076 --> 00:35:22,245
It's her job.

535
00:35:22,579 --> 00:35:24,205
She has to do it.
What's cute about that?

536
00:35:24,581 --> 00:35:27,292
She seems sharp,
but she's also adorably clueless.

537
00:35:27,792 --> 00:35:30,211
Was she like that when you went
on that blind date with her?

538
00:35:32,505 --> 00:35:33,632
I don't know.

539
00:35:36,051 --> 00:35:38,928
Don't be so prickly with her.
Be nice to her, okay?

540
00:35:39,179 --> 00:35:40,764
If she runs away because of you

541
00:35:40,847 --> 00:35:42,557
I'm seriously going to disappear
and travel around Europe.

542
00:35:44,392 --> 00:35:45,477
Just drink.

543
00:35:48,813 --> 00:35:49,856
Excuse me, Auntie.

544
00:35:50,148 --> 00:35:51,941
Could you put some garlic
in a little dish for me?

545
00:35:52,025 --> 00:35:54,861
- Okay.
- Minced, please. Thank you.

546
00:35:56,780 --> 00:35:59,574
Who eats <i>sundae gukbap</i>
when they're on a diet?

547
00:36:01,159 --> 00:36:02,369
It's my cheat day.

548
00:36:03,870 --> 00:36:05,330
Thank you.

549
00:36:05,664 --> 00:36:06,665
Me too.

550
00:36:07,123 --> 00:36:09,292
What's gotten into you?

551
00:36:09,376 --> 00:36:12,295
You're drinking on a weekday.

552
00:36:13,880 --> 00:36:14,881
Here.

553
00:36:21,096 --> 00:36:22,389
Did something happen?

554
00:36:24,015 --> 00:36:25,266
- Auntie.
- Yes?

555
00:36:25,892 --> 00:36:26,893
I kissed someone.

556
00:36:27,602 --> 00:36:30,397
- Oh, garlic's gotten expensive.
- It's fresh garlic.

557
00:36:31,147 --> 00:36:33,233
Garlic prices are
practically gold these days.

558
00:36:33,650 --> 00:36:35,151
Ki...

559
00:36:35,235 --> 00:36:36,986
- Prices have gone through the roof.
- A kiss?

560
00:36:39,197 --> 00:36:41,116
Hey, what the...

561
00:36:41,199 --> 00:36:43,034
You joined
such an open-minded company

562
00:36:43,118 --> 00:36:44,619
and now you're getting all radical.

563
00:36:46,746 --> 00:36:47,747
With whom?

564
00:36:50,208 --> 00:36:51,960
Was it that blind date guy?

565
00:36:59,050 --> 00:37:00,385
In my opinion

566
00:37:01,803 --> 00:37:03,388
that blind date guy is

567
00:37:04,305 --> 00:37:05,306
your <i>malatang</i>.

568
00:37:05,890 --> 00:37:06,891
But wait.

569
00:37:08,727 --> 00:37:10,687
Where? No, I mean...

570
00:37:11,229 --> 00:37:12,397
How did it happen?

571
00:37:12,689 --> 00:37:13,982
No, not that.

572
00:37:14,524 --> 00:37:15,567
Did you like it?

573
00:37:18,528 --> 00:37:20,447
I don't know.

574
00:37:20,530 --> 00:37:21,614
You must've liked it.

575
00:37:23,825 --> 00:37:26,286
Oh, you lucky girl.

576
00:37:27,704 --> 00:37:28,955
I told you, it's not like that.

577
00:37:30,039 --> 00:37:31,583
This is driving me crazy.

578
00:37:31,666 --> 00:37:35,378
Did you like it so much
that you keep thinking about it?

579
00:37:35,795 --> 00:37:39,340
Do your toes get all tingly, itchy,
and restless, it's driving you nuts?

580
00:37:40,675 --> 00:37:42,969
I told you it was a kiss
with no feelings involved.

581
00:37:43,052 --> 00:37:46,014
If there are no feelings,
there's no way my body would do that.

582
00:37:46,097 --> 00:37:47,432
And besides, that man...

583
00:37:55,148 --> 00:37:56,232
He's gay.

584
00:37:56,316 --> 00:37:58,401
What are you saying?
Speak up. I can't hear you.

585
00:38:00,111 --> 00:38:01,154
He's gay.

586
00:38:02,405 --> 00:38:03,990
He likes men, not women.

587
00:38:06,242 --> 00:38:07,744
What?

588
00:38:08,536 --> 00:38:09,537
A gay?

589
00:38:12,248 --> 00:38:13,416
Gay...

590
00:38:42,153 --> 00:38:44,155
ARE YOU BUSY?
LET'S MEET UP SOME TIME

591
00:38:46,491 --> 00:38:48,743
LEAVE CHATROOM

592
00:38:50,453 --> 00:38:52,580
GONG YEON-SU

593
00:39:49,554 --> 00:39:51,222
Wait, isn't that Nam-su over there?

594
00:39:52,515 --> 00:39:53,558
Where?

595
00:39:53,641 --> 00:39:55,935
I thought I just saw him
on the screen.

596
00:39:58,730 --> 00:39:59,814
That can't be.

597
00:40:00,189 --> 00:40:02,525
Why would a studying kid
be at a concert?

598
00:40:04,110 --> 00:40:05,153
I see.

599
00:40:58,206 --> 00:40:59,999
Oh, my goodness.

600
00:41:08,549 --> 00:41:10,510
It's better than I thought.

601
00:41:10,969 --> 00:41:12,512
Now my shoulders.

602
00:41:20,520 --> 00:41:22,397
THE TEMPERATURE OF LOVE
IN BODY LANGUAGE

603
00:41:22,480 --> 00:41:24,524
My shoulders are so tense.

604
00:41:25,441 --> 00:41:26,859
It's less crowded than I expected.

605
00:41:27,193 --> 00:41:30,405
Right? It's not exactly the kind
of place families come on weekends.

606
00:41:31,322 --> 00:41:33,866
See? I'm all you have, right?

607
00:42:12,071 --> 00:42:13,072
Mr. Yun...

608
00:42:20,329 --> 00:42:22,665
What? They came together.

609
00:42:28,588 --> 00:42:32,550
Well, it is the weekend.
I guess they're on a date.

610
00:42:36,846 --> 00:42:38,598
Let's not awkwardly tag along.

611
00:42:39,682 --> 00:42:40,767
I should go.

612
00:42:42,977 --> 00:42:44,854
Hey, Yeon-su.

613
00:42:46,522 --> 00:42:48,524
You came to see this too.

614
00:42:48,816 --> 00:42:50,777
If I'd known,
I would've asked you to come with us.

615
00:42:50,860 --> 00:42:52,403
Oh, no.

616
00:42:52,487 --> 00:42:56,949
I just finished looking around
and was about to leave.

617
00:42:57,658 --> 00:42:59,577
But this is the direction
the exhibit starts from.

618
00:43:02,080 --> 00:43:05,416
Oh, I guess
I was going the wrong way.

619
00:43:07,126 --> 00:43:08,586
Since you're here,
you might as well stick around.

620
00:43:09,045 --> 00:43:10,421
It might be fun to see it together.

621
00:43:10,963 --> 00:43:12,632
- Let's go.
- Okay.

622
00:43:24,977 --> 00:43:28,022
There's snow falling
behind the man's head

623
00:43:28,856 --> 00:43:30,858
while there are flowers blooming
behind the woman's back.

624
00:43:31,859 --> 00:43:32,985
I wonder what it means.

625
00:43:36,656 --> 00:43:41,786
Maybe they were in love
until winter passed and spring came.

626
00:43:42,453 --> 00:43:43,871
That makes sense.

627
00:43:43,955 --> 00:43:46,165
Love is like the seasons, after all.

628
00:43:47,708 --> 00:43:48,709
What do you think, Dal?

629
00:43:50,461 --> 00:43:53,840
The man has his eyes open,
while the woman has hers closed.

630
00:43:53,923 --> 00:43:56,843
It means he's bored enough
to stare blankly into space.

631
00:43:57,135 --> 00:43:59,220
And she's lost in her own world
without even realizing it.

632
00:43:59,804 --> 00:44:02,557
One side is frozen
while the other is blooming.

633
00:44:03,015 --> 00:44:04,725
I think it represents
the state of their hearts.

634
00:44:05,017 --> 00:44:06,602
This isn't love.

635
00:44:06,894 --> 00:44:07,895
It's a tragedy.

636
00:44:11,399 --> 00:44:15,653
Did something happen today
to put you in a bad mood?

637
00:44:16,112 --> 00:44:18,239
- No.
- Yeon-su, just let him be.

638
00:44:18,322 --> 00:44:19,740
I shouldn't have asked.

639
00:44:24,078 --> 00:44:27,832
How do you manage to be negative

640
00:44:28,541 --> 00:44:30,835
about love every time?

641
00:44:32,670 --> 00:44:34,505
I'm not being negative.
I'm being realistic.

642
00:44:35,590 --> 00:44:38,634
The essence of what humans call love

643
00:44:39,051 --> 00:44:41,220
is ultimately based on the desire
to reproduce.

644
00:44:42,138 --> 00:44:45,057
You could say
it's a kind of hormonal response

645
00:44:45,141 --> 00:44:46,934
from the urge to increase
the chances of reproduction.

646
00:44:47,643 --> 00:44:49,312
Oh, here we go again.

647
00:44:49,395 --> 00:44:51,606
The human brain isn't that romantic.

648
00:44:54,692 --> 00:44:56,819
You can become attached to one person

649
00:44:57,320 --> 00:44:59,655
and still feel sexual desires
for a stranger.

650
00:45:23,471 --> 00:45:25,806
ILLUSION
SOMETHING YOU CAN'T GRASP OR CONTAIN

651
00:45:28,643 --> 00:45:30,228
You don't know
what to do either, do you?

652
00:45:30,645 --> 00:45:33,314
What to put inside.

653
00:45:34,774 --> 00:45:37,860
Whether it's feelings or desire

654
00:45:38,402 --> 00:45:40,154
I don't have a clue either.

655
00:45:45,493 --> 00:45:47,828
PUT YOUR HAND INSIDE
WHAT YOU GRASP IS WHAT YOU DESIRE

656
00:46:00,216 --> 00:46:02,718
LOVE IS THEREFORE A RED TRAFFIC LIGHT

657
00:46:13,104 --> 00:46:14,563
How about
a buy-one-get-one-free event?

658
00:46:14,647 --> 00:46:16,983
Buy one men's toy
and get a women's toy free.

659
00:46:17,066 --> 00:46:19,193
The world isn't made up
of just male-female couples.

660
00:46:19,485 --> 00:46:22,280
Targeting only certain couples
doesn't suit our identity.

661
00:46:22,363 --> 00:46:23,698
What do you think, Yeon-su?

662
00:46:24,407 --> 00:46:27,243
A flashy event
might grab people's attention

663
00:46:27,326 --> 00:46:29,412
but marketing needs
to capture their hearts.

664
00:46:30,204 --> 00:46:31,789
For attention to lead to a purchase

665
00:46:31,872 --> 00:46:33,916
we first need to spark curiosity
about the product.

666
00:46:35,251 --> 00:46:37,503
So I had an idea.

667
00:46:39,588 --> 00:46:40,631
Random.

668
00:46:42,008 --> 00:46:44,510
- "Random"?
- We use the excitement

669
00:46:44,593 --> 00:46:46,095
that comes from the unexpected.

670
00:46:46,178 --> 00:46:47,722
Like a mystery box.

671
00:46:47,805 --> 00:46:49,015
I'm not sure I follow.

672
00:46:49,307 --> 00:46:52,810
We pick out products for people
who don't know what they should buy.

673
00:46:52,893 --> 00:46:55,479
But why would anyone buy something
when they don't know what's inside?

674
00:46:55,938 --> 00:46:57,231
That's exactly why they buy it.

675
00:46:57,732 --> 00:46:59,317
I'd totally want one.

676
00:46:59,400 --> 00:47:02,194
Aren't you dying to know
what's inside?

677
00:47:02,278 --> 00:47:05,281
The concept itself is so sexy.

678
00:47:05,364 --> 00:47:08,075
But sex toys are
such a matter of personal preference.

679
00:47:08,159 --> 00:47:09,702
So we'd need to build a database.

680
00:47:10,202 --> 00:47:12,371
Married couples, couples, or singles

681
00:47:12,455 --> 00:47:14,749
from their individual preferences
to their sexual fantasies.

682
00:47:15,333 --> 00:47:16,584
- Right?
- Yes.

683
00:47:16,834 --> 00:47:18,878
We could also customize
the contents based on concepts

684
00:47:18,961 --> 00:47:21,547
like sexless couples,
couples going through a rough patch

685
00:47:21,630 --> 00:47:23,341
or a masturbation kit.

686
00:47:24,967 --> 00:47:26,135
Sounds good.

687
00:47:26,218 --> 00:47:28,262
It's almost too good
to use for just an event.

688
00:47:28,346 --> 00:47:29,347
Sounds like fun.

689
00:47:31,474 --> 00:47:34,101
But how did you come up
with such an idea?

690
00:47:34,352 --> 00:47:36,354
At the art museum last time.

691
00:47:36,604 --> 00:47:39,231
There was a box
in one of the installations.

692
00:47:39,315 --> 00:47:42,902
You could randomly pull out
a piece of paper with a note on it.

693
00:47:43,235 --> 00:47:44,362
I got curious

694
00:47:44,570 --> 00:47:48,616
and the message I happened to pick
really resonated with me.

695
00:47:49,116 --> 00:47:52,203
- That's why.
- You can watch the same thing

696
00:47:52,620 --> 00:47:54,497
and one person gets bored
while another gets inspired.

697
00:47:55,498 --> 00:47:56,707
That's why she's a pro.

698
00:47:57,416 --> 00:47:58,876
You're a professional for a reason.

699
00:48:08,386 --> 00:48:10,638
Then let's go with the random box.

700
00:48:10,721 --> 00:48:13,099
- Yes.
- All right.

701
00:48:13,933 --> 00:48:16,769
How about we discuss
the specific products over some beer?

702
00:48:16,852 --> 00:48:19,188
- Love it.
- Let's go right now. Sounds great.

703
00:48:19,271 --> 00:48:21,440
Let's go. Let's wrap things up.

704
00:48:21,524 --> 00:48:22,691
I heard that place was really good.

705
00:48:22,775 --> 00:48:25,069
That place we went to was so good.
Why did it close down?

706
00:48:25,152 --> 00:48:26,904
- Where?
- You know.

707
00:48:26,987 --> 00:48:28,572
- You haven't tried it?
- I didn't go with you.

708
00:48:28,656 --> 00:48:29,740
It was really good.

709
00:48:29,824 --> 00:48:30,950
You're not sulking, are you?

710
00:48:31,409 --> 00:48:32,535
Excuse me.

711
00:48:33,619 --> 00:48:35,871
I'll head home first.

712
00:48:35,955 --> 00:48:38,040
Why? You came all the way here.

713
00:48:38,999 --> 00:48:41,293
I'm suddenly not feeling very well.

714
00:48:41,669 --> 00:48:43,254
Well, that's a buzzkill.

715
00:48:43,337 --> 00:48:45,423
You were supposed
to be the star tonight.

716
00:48:45,506 --> 00:48:48,384
- I'm sorry. I'll join next...
- It can't be helped.

717
00:48:48,467 --> 00:48:49,468
Go on, then.

718
00:48:50,928 --> 00:48:52,054
Right.

719
00:48:52,888 --> 00:48:54,348
Okay, then.

720
00:48:54,432 --> 00:48:56,392
Should I take you home?

721
00:48:56,475 --> 00:48:57,685
Oh, no.

722
00:48:58,644 --> 00:49:00,438
I'll go by myself.

723
00:49:00,813 --> 00:49:02,398
Oh, what a shame.

724
00:49:05,734 --> 00:49:08,320
Let's go inside
and raise a glass to ourselves.

725
00:49:08,404 --> 00:49:09,613
- Come on, Mr. Yun.
- Let's go!

726
00:49:09,697 --> 00:49:12,158
- You should lead the way.
- All right. Let's go.

727
00:49:12,241 --> 00:49:14,452
- Lead the way.
- Hey, let's go.

728
00:49:18,164 --> 00:49:19,999
He must've felt uncomfortable too.

729
00:49:20,291 --> 00:49:22,626
He brushed me off like
he'd been waiting for the chance.

730
00:49:23,377 --> 00:49:27,173
Why does he get to do that?
I should've been the one to do it.

731
00:49:33,012 --> 00:49:34,305
Darn it.

732
00:50:05,461 --> 00:50:07,171
You walk fast.

733
00:50:08,047 --> 00:50:09,048
What about dinner?

734
00:50:09,715 --> 00:50:11,133
It was canceled because of someone.

735
00:50:13,636 --> 00:50:15,179
Why don't we find shelter over there?

736
00:50:44,124 --> 00:50:45,918
Are you feeling okay?

737
00:50:49,630 --> 00:50:52,591
- I'm fine.
- Did you review the contract?

738
00:50:55,135 --> 00:50:58,639
Are you really bringing up
the contract here?

739
00:51:01,892 --> 00:51:03,394
Then what am I
supposed to talk about?

740
00:51:06,355 --> 00:51:07,606
Why did you do it?

741
00:51:08,732 --> 00:51:09,984
That day.

742
00:51:11,569 --> 00:51:13,237
Why did you kiss me?

743
00:51:20,953 --> 00:51:22,454
I just wanted to.

744
00:51:22,997 --> 00:51:24,164
With you, Yeon-su.

745
00:51:25,040 --> 00:51:26,041
<i>I know...</i>

746
00:51:27,084 --> 00:51:29,712
I apologize
if it made you feel uncomfortable.

747
00:51:30,129 --> 00:51:32,631
<i>...that I shouldn't be doing this</i>
<i>with him.</i>

748
00:51:33,257 --> 00:51:34,383
<i>However...</i>

749
00:51:36,510 --> 00:51:38,304
I'm really sorry

750
00:51:38,971 --> 00:51:41,432
but there's something
I have to confirm.

751
00:51:43,350 --> 00:51:45,311
Please forgive my rudeness.

752
00:51:45,519 --> 00:51:47,146
- Sorry?
- Then...

753
00:51:48,022 --> 00:51:50,316
Excuse me for a moment.

754
00:52:41,492 --> 00:52:43,243
<i>CONTRADICTION</i>
BY YANG GUI-JA

755
00:52:43,327 --> 00:52:45,162
LOVE IS THEREFORE A RED TRAFFIC LIGHT

756
00:52:45,245 --> 00:52:47,039
YOU MUST STOP THE MOMENT IT TURNS ON

757
00:52:47,122 --> 00:52:48,832
IT WARNS OF DANGER
WHILE ALSO SIGNALING SAFETY

758
00:52:48,916 --> 00:52:52,586
THAT RED TRAFFIC LIGHT IS LOVE

759
00:53:20,489 --> 00:53:23,659
- Oh, no.
- Wait...

760
00:53:25,202 --> 00:53:27,413
- Ms. Gong?
- Mr. Dokgo.

761
00:53:28,288 --> 00:53:31,083
Why are you doing this to me?

762
00:53:32,167 --> 00:53:33,502
What do you mean?

763
00:53:33,877 --> 00:53:35,170
You started it this time.

764
00:53:36,880 --> 00:53:38,465
Mr. Dokgo.

765
00:53:40,050 --> 00:53:41,885
But you're gay.

766
00:53:52,438 --> 00:53:53,439
I'm sorry?

767
00:53:53,772 --> 00:53:58,152
<i>And yet, I want to feel</i>
<i>every part of this stranger.</i>

768
00:54:06,285 --> 00:54:10,247
MAKE ME TINGLE

769
00:54:26,221 --> 00:54:28,223
<i>Let's prepare the other ingredients.</i>

770
00:54:28,766 --> 00:54:30,684
<i>I like zucchini</i>

771
00:54:30,768 --> 00:54:33,604
<i>so I'll dice up</i>
<i>about a quarter of one.</i>

772
00:54:34,438 --> 00:54:37,941
<i>Chop the onion and green onion</i>
<i>and set them aside.</i>

773
00:54:38,567 --> 00:54:40,152
<i>When making the broth</i>

774
00:54:40,235 --> 00:54:43,447
